   "title": "Scatter and copy (read me)",
   "properties": {
    "text": ""
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "Scatter points on a surface and copy a model onto every point.\n\n1) Grid + Attribute Noise (terrain fractal, Y only) make rolling ground.\n2) Scatter puts 250 random points on it.\n3) Attribute Randomize writes two point attributes that Copy to Points reads: pscale (uniform size, 0.15 to 0.6) and orient (a random rotation quaternion).\n4) The 'rock' is a coarse sphere roughened by Point Jitter.\n5) Copy to Points places one rock per point, scaled by pscale and rotated by orient. Merge adds the ground back for the preview.\n\nTweak: Scatter Count and Seed, the pscale Min / Max, the jitter Scale, or swap the sphere for any other geometry."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653"
  },
